# PR 2 — the Breakdown panel (steps 5–9)

## Step 5 — session sums in `internal/agentusage` · S (parallel with PR 1)

**Files:** new `internal/agentusage/breakdown.go`, new
`internal/agentusage/breakdown_test.go`; `docs/architecture/agent-usage.md`.

```go
// Categories is a session's tokens by kind, the cache writes split by cache
// lifetime.
type Categories struct {
	Input, Output, CacheWrite5m, CacheWrite1h, CacheRead int64
}

// Total is the sum of the five, saturating at math.MaxInt64.
func (c Categories) Total() int64

// Categories sums every agent's tokens by kind. Input, Output, CacheRead and
// the total cache write come from Agent.Tokens (so the total equals
// Usage.Total().Total()); the 1 h part is the sum of ByModel's CacheWrite1h,
// clamped to the total write; the 5 min part is the rest. An agent without
// ByModel counts all its writes as 5 min.
func (u Usage) Categories() Categories

// ModelTotals merges every agent's ByModel by exact model name. An agent with
// tokens and no ByModel adds its tokens to the "" bucket (as pricing.Agent
// does). Order: tokens descending, then name; the "" bucket last.
func (u Usage) ModelTotals() []ModelUsage
```

**Tests** (`go test ./internal/agentusage -run 'TestCategories|TestModelTotals'`):
empty usage; `Categories().Total() == Total().Total()`; `5m + 1h == Total().CacheWrite`;
Σ `ModelTotals` == `Total()` field-wise; same model in two agents merged; `""` bucket
merged and last; agent without `ByModel` → `""`, 5 min; 1 h above the write clamped;
`MaxInt64` counters → no panic, fields ≥ 0; fixture `testdata/v2.1.302-cost/` agrees with
`ParseSession`'s `ByModel`; one case through `Aggregate` equals the full parse.

## Step 6 — the breakdown model (pure, view side) · S (depends on 5)

**Files:** new `internal/ui/agentusageview/breakdown.go`, new `breakdown_test.go`.

```go
// breakdownLine is one entry of a block.
type breakdownLine struct {
	label  string
	role   theme.TokenRole // category block only: the swatch colour; "" elsewhere
	tokens int64
	tenths int // noShare when the session has no token
}

type breakdownBlock struct {
	title string // "By category", "By model", "By agent"
	lines []breakdownLine
	total int64 // == Usage.Total().Total()
}

type breakdown struct{ blocks []breakdownBlock }

// buildBreakdown builds the three blocks of u; rows are agentRows' output, in
// canonical order, whatever the table's sort and filter.
func buildBreakdown(u agentusage.Usage, rows []agentRow) breakdown

// largestIndex is the index of the largest value, the first on a tie; -1 when empty.
func largestIndex(values []int64) int
```

Category block: `Input`, `Output`, `Cache write 5 min`, `Cache write 1 h`, `Cache read`
(both writes take the cache-write role); residue to the largest. Model block:
`u.ModelTotals()`, `unknown` for `""`; residue to the largest. Agent block: `orchestrator`
or `<type> <idCell(r)>`; `tenths = r.share`.

**Tests** (`-run 'TestBuildBreakdown|TestLargestIndex'`): each block sums to 1000 (AC4)
on several usages; Σ tokens == `u.Total().Total()`; agent block == Share column;
zero-token session → `noShare`, no panic (AC5); `unknown` last; two coders → two IDs;
only types, IDs, model names and numbers reach the panel (AC7); `[1,1,1]` → `[334,333,333]`.

## Step 7 — panel rendering and scrolling (pure) · M (depends on 6 and 2)

**Files:** new `internal/ui/agentusageview/breakdown_view.go`, new `breakdown_view_test.go`.

```go
// renderBreakdown renders the panel as lines exactly width cells wide,
// measured as plain text and styled afterwards (Rule 122). A block is a header
// line (title, "Share", "Tokens"; ColorSecondary bold, Rule 118), its lines and
// a "Total 100.0% <tokens>" line; blocks are separated by theme.EmptyLineBg.
// A category line starts with a one-cell swatch — theme.GaugeFill(1) in its
// role's TokenStyle — the bar's colour legend. Zeros and "-" are DimStyle.
func renderBreakdown(b breakdown, width int) []string

// clampTop keeps a scroll offset within [0, max(0, lines-height)].
func clampTop(top, lines, height int) int
```

Layout: 1 cell padding, swatch + space (category block), label (rest, `…`), 2 spaces,
share right-aligned in 6, 2 spaces, tokens right-aligned in max(6, longest). Under 8
cells of label the Tokens column goes, then Share; always exactly `width`.

**Tests** (`-run 'TestRenderBreakdown|TestClampTop'`): exact width at 198, 118, 78, 58,
38, 22, 10, 1; three titles in order, `Total` / `100.0%` per block; swatch colours ==
`theme.TokenColor` of each category line (Cache write 5 min and 1 h the same); narrow
widths drop columns; zero-token session shows `-`; long model name truncated with `…`;
`clampTop` `(5,10,20)→0`, `(15,30,20)→10`, `(-3,30,20)→0`, `(0,0,0)→0`.

## Step 8 — tabs, keys, footer, header, help · M/L (depends on 7)

**Files:** `model.go`, `update.go`, `selection.go`, `view.go`, `availability.go`,
`help.go`; tests in new `breakdown_tab_test.go`, plus `availability_test.go`,
`agentusageview_test.go`, `header_live_test.go`, `cost_test.go`, `cost_summary_test.go`.

```go
type agentsTab int

const (
	tabAgents agentsTab = iota
	tabBreakdown
)

// Model gains: tab agentsTab; breakdown breakdown (rebuilt by withRows);
// breakdownTop int (clamped in Update).

// actions gains: Tab (unavailable at the sessions level), Filter and Sort
// (unavailable on the Breakdown tab).
const (
	reasonNoTabs            = "No tabs at the session list"
	reasonBreakdownNoFilter = "The breakdown covers the whole session — switch to Agents to filter"
	reasonBreakdownNoSort   = "Nothing to sort in the breakdown"
)

func (m Model) switchTab() (tea.Model, tea.Cmd)
func (m Model) scrollBreakdown(key string) (tea.Model, tea.Cmd)
func (m Model) tabRow(width int) string
// headerRows: the visible rows on Agents, every row on Breakdown (Q4).
func (m Model) headerRows() []agentRow
```

`handleKey`: edit mode → `ctrl+r` → `tab`/`shift+tab` (silent guard on `a.Tab`) → on
Breakdown: scroll keys, `/` and `.` through `guard`, `←`/`esc`/`→`/`enter` as today, the
rest ignored → Agents: today's behaviour. Cases over 5 lines become `handle…` methods
(Rule 201). `View()`: Breakdown tab → the clamped window of `renderBreakdown(m.breakdown,
m.width-2)`; otherwise unchanged (Rule 139). `GetShortcuts()`: `ctrl+r`, `→`, `esc`,
`tab Switch tab`, `/`, `.`, `?`.

**Tests** (`-run 'TestBreakdownTab|TestAgentsLevelAdvertises|TestShortcut|TestFooter|TestBreadcrumb|TestHelp'`):
seven identical keys in every state (update `TestAgentsLevelAdvertisesTheSameSixKeys`
and its "`.` never greyed", now "never greyed on Agents nor at the sessions level");
greying per state; `tab` at the sessions level: nothing happens, no message; `/` and
`.` on Breakdown: Warn with the reason, no state change; round trip Agents → Breakdown
→ Agents keeps cursor, sort and filter; scroll with 40 sub-agents at height 20; live
deltas update the panel, offset clamped (AC6); filter ignored by the panel (AC6);
header `Tokens` == panel totals on Breakdown, filtered on Agents (AC4, Q4); footer
heights 2 / 4 / 6 / 4 and line count == `GetFooterHeight()`; footer order (Q1, replaces
`TestBreadcrumbSitsAboveTheFilterBar`); `FilterBarVisible()` and `InEditMode()` false
on Breakdown; open from Breakdown lands on Agents; zero-token panel (AC5); help lists
`tab` and the Breakdown section; `go test -count=2` and `mise run test-race`.

## Step 9 — docs · S (help in step 8's commit, Rule 114)

- `help.go`: key `tab`; section **Breakdown**: the bar (colours as a legend in words,
  order, fixed width, the glyph from `app.gauge_glyph`, rounding, `-`, colour only — the
  exact figures are in the columns and the Breakdown tab), the panel (three blocks, % of
  **tokens**, residue rules, `unknown`, whole session, ignores the filter, live, scroll
  keys), counters only; how to retune the four colours in a theme file.
- `docs/architecture/agent-usage.md`: Public API (`Categories`, `ModelTotals`);
  "Per-model tokens"; the Breakdown column, drop order, `apportion`'s doctrine, the
  `Spans` use; subsection "Breakdown tab (DEVDESK-98)".
- `docs/architecture/ui-components.md`: `Column.Spans` (if not done in step 3).
- `.claude/CLAUDE.md`: agent-usage paragraph of the Overview and the `agent-usage.md`
  row of the Architecture table.
- `docs/backlog.md`: decision **D93** (Plane DEVDESK-98): tabs; `tab`; colour-only bar on
  the gauge glyph (AC3 replaced, with the reason); `Spans` in `datatable`; four token
  roles and their tests; column place and drop order; footer order; header on the
  Breakdown tab; tab reset on open.
- `docs/product/agent-usage-monitor/stories.md`: S-10 criterion 3 amended, questions
  answered (the Plane work item too — pm).

**Done when:** **PR 2**: `feat: break down a session's tokens by category, model and
agent (DEVDESK-98)`.

---

## Dependencies and parallelism

```
1 ─┐
2 ─┼─► 4                          (PR 1)
3 ─┘
5 ──► 6 ──► 7 ──► 8 ──► 9         (PR 2; 7 also needs 2)
```

Steps 1, 2, 3 and 5 are independent. Steps 6 and 7 only add files. Step 8 starts after
PR 1 is merged, on a worktree cut from the new `main`.

## Risks and irreversible points

1. **`datatable` is shared by every table.** `Spans` must not change any existing
   rendering: the split-run and render tests stay green unchanged, and `renderRuns`
   factoring is checked against them before `Spans` is added.
2. **Colour-only reading (AC3 replaced).** No colour (`NO_COLOR`, a 16-colour terminal,
   a colour-vision deficiency): the bar shows only "has tokens". Mitigation: the count
   columns and the Breakdown tab; declared in Rule 122's exception and in the help.

